{"name":"Blue Potato","hex":"#64617b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue potato","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A potato characterized by its blue or purple skin and flesh (a result of high concentrations of anthocyanins) and earthy, slightly sweet flavor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_potato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Potato","blocks":[{"text":"The potato is a starchy tuberous vegetable native to the Americas that is consumed as a staple food in many parts of the world. Potatoes are underground stem tubers of the plant Solanum tuberosum, a perennial in the nightshade family Solanaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato","wikidata":"Q10998"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/CIP-Afiche-papa-ingles.jpg/500px-CIP-Afiche-papa-ingles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte